{"from":"1:1","body":"<p><ref to=\"2TI.1.1\">1</ref> Paul's love to Timothy, and the unfeigned faith which was in Timothy himself, his mother, and grandmother.<br/><ref to=\"2TI.1.6\">6</ref> He is exhorted to stir up the gift of God which was in him;<br/><ref to=\"2TI.1.8\">8</ref> to be stedfast and patient in persecution;<br/><ref to=\"2TI.1.13\">13</ref> and to persist in the form and truth of that doctrine which he had learned of him.<br/><ref to=\"2TI.1.15\">15</ref> Phygellus and Hermogenes, and such like, are noted, and Onesiphorus is highly commended.<br/><br/><br/>an.<br/><ref to=\"ROM.1.1 2CO.1.1\">Ro 1:1; 2Co 1:1</ref><br/>the promise.<br/><ref to=\"JHN.5.24 JHN.5.39 JHN.5.40 JHN.6.40 JHN.6.54 JHN.10.28 JHN.17.3 ROM.5.21 ROM.6.23 2CO.1.20\">Joh 5:24,39,40; 6:40,54; 10:28; 17:3; Ro 5:21; 6:23; 2Co 1:20</ref><br/><ref to=\"EPH.3.6 TIT.1.2 HEB.9.15 2PE.1.3 2PE.1.4 1JN.2.25 1JN.5.11-1JN.5.13\">Eph 3:6; Tit 1:2; Heb 9:15; 2Pe 1:3,4; 1Jo 2:25; 5:11-13</ref></p>"}
